  "title": "Introducing Spend Caps for Billing Budgets",
  "summary": "Cloud Billing Budgets now supports a new `spendCap` feature, allowing you to define and enforce spending limits directly within your budgets. This introduces a new `SpendCap` schema with `inputState` for control and `outputState` for monitoring.",
  "details": "A significant new capability has been added to the Cloud Billing Budgets API: the `GoogleCloudBillingBudgetsV1Budget` schema now includes an optional `spendCap` property. This new `GoogleCloudBillingBudgetsV1SpendCap` schema allows you to configure and manage spending limits.\n\nKey properties of `SpendCap` include `inputState`, which you can set to `CONFIGURED` to activate the cap or `AWAITING_NEXT_PERIOD` to lift an enforced cap. The `outputState` and `reconciling` fields are strictly output-only, providing the actual state and processing status of the spend cap. Attempts to set these fields will result in an error.\n\nBe aware that enabling a `spendCap` introduces new restrictions on other budget properties: `ownershipScope` must be `OWNERSHIP_SCOPE_UNSPECIFIED` or `ALL_USERS` (not `BILLING_ACCOUNT`), and `spendBasis` cannot be `FORECASTED_SPEND` within `ThresholdRule`.",
